        <section id="why-choose-us" class="py-3">
            <h2 class="pipe">Premier Commercial & Residential Asphalt Paving in Concord, MA</h2>
            <p>At <strong>S. Phaneuf & Associates</strong>, we deliver top-tier commercial parking lot paving, roadway resurfacing, and luxury residential driveway construction throughout <strong>Concord, Massachusetts</strong>. With over 35 years of civil contracting experience, our crew understands the rigorous demands of Concord's soil conditions and winter freeze-thaw cycles.</p>
            <p>Whether you manage a commercial retail center near Route 2, an HOA residential community, or a private estate in Concord, we engineer durable asphalt pavement structures designed to withstand heavy wheel loads, snowplow friction, and severe thermal expansion.</p>
            
            <h3 class="c-b mt-5">Our Concord Asphalt Paving Capabilities</h3>
            <ul class="lst-n ps-0">
                <li class="mb-3"><strong>Commercial Parking Lot Construction & Milling:</strong> Full-depth pavement installation, asphalt milling, reclaimed aggregate sub-base leveling, and ADA-compliant parking stalls.</li>
                <li class="mb-3"><strong>Custom Residential Estate Driveways:</strong> Dense-graded binder course paired with smooth top-coat asphalt, cobblestone aprons, and granite curbing.</li>
                <li class="mb-3"><strong>Asphalt Berms & Cape Cod Berms:</strong> Extruded asphalt berms engineered to control runoff water, protect lawns from wheel damage, and preserve driveway borders.</li>
                <li class="mb-3"><strong>Resurfacing & Overlay Services:</strong> Cost-effective pavement rejuvenation that repairs surface oxidation, potholes, and alligator cracking without full excavation.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="paving-process" class="py-3">
            <h2 class="pipe">The Engineering Behind Durable Concord Asphalt</h2>
            <p>Long-lasting asphalt paving starts beneath the surface. S. Phaneuf & Associates adheres to strict Massachusetts Department of Transportation (MassDOT) material standards for sub-base preparation and compaction:</p>
            <ol class="ps-4">
                <li class="mb-2"><strong>Subgrade Excavation & Geotextile Stabilization:</strong> Unstable subsoil is removed, compacted, and reinforced with heavy-duty geotextile fabric.</li>
                <li class="mb-2"><strong>Crushed Aggregate Base Course:</strong> A dense 4-to-8 inch processed gravel base is compacted with heavy vibratory rollers to achieve maximum load-bearing density.</li>
                <li class="mb-2"><strong>Hot Mix Asphalt (HMA) Application:</strong> Commercial-grade binder and top courses are applied at high temperatures for optimal bitumen bonding.</li>
                <li class="mb-2"><strong>Precision Edge & Berm Extrusion:</strong> Cape Cod berms or concrete curbing are sealed to prevent moisture infiltration under the pavement base.</li>
            </ol>
        </section>

        <section id="faqs" class="py-3">
            <h2 class="pipe">Frequently Asked Questions About Paving in Concord, MA</h2>
            <p>Here are answers to common questions about asphalt driveway and commercial parking lot paving in Concord, Massachusetts:</p>
            
            <h3 class="fw-0 pt-3">Q: How much does commercial parking lot or residential driveway paving cost in Concord, MA?</h3>
            <p>A: Costs depend on total square footage, subgrade soil preparation, asphalt layer thickness (binder vs. top course), and custom features like Cape Cod berms or cobblestone aprons. We provide free on-site estimates tailored to your project specs.</p>
            
            <h3 class="fw-0 pt-3">Q: How long does a newly paved asphalt driveway last in New England?</h3>
            <p>A: With a properly compacted aggregate base and proper drainage, professionally installed asphalt in Concord lasts 20 to 30 years. Regular sealcoating protects against oxidation and winter freeze-thaw damage.</p>
            
            <h3 class="fw-0 pt-3">Q: What is the difference between asphalt resurfacing (overlay) and full excavation?</h3>
            <p>A: Resurfacing applies a fresh layer of hot-mix asphalt over existing structurally sound pavement. Full-depth excavation is required when the underlying aggregate base is failing or severely damaged by frost heave.</p>
            
            <h3 class="fw-0 pt-3">Q: Do I need a town permit for driveway paving or commercial parking lot construction in Concord, MA?</h3>
            <p>A: Residential driveway repaving within existing footprints usually does not require permits. Commercial parking lots, apron curb cuts, or projects affecting stormwater runoff near public roads may require town approval. We manage necessary permit filings for you.</p>

            <h3 class="fw-0 pt-3">Q: Can you install extruded Cape Cod berms or cobblestone aprons?</h3>
            <p>A: Yes! Extruded asphalt Cape Cod berms and granite cobblestone aprons are popular additions in Concord that protect lawn edges and control rainwater runoff effectively.</p>
        </section>

